It seems the definition for pam entitlement approval workflow wasn't quite right, it was causing the entitlement to be replaced each time even if the definition wasn't changed.
(see job here: https://github.com/populationgenomics/cpg-infrastructure-private/actions/runs/20904895199/job/60056657294)

The preview diff shows it attempting to add the approvalWorkflow section even though it hasn't changed

```
 +-gcp:privilegedaccessmanager/entitlement:entitlement: (replace)
     [id=projects/<id>/locations/global/entitlements/pam-<project>-read]
     [urn=urn:pulumi:production::datasets::gcp:privilegedaccessmanager/entitlement:entitlement::<project>-gcp-temporary-bucket-access-main-read]
     [provider=urn:pulumi:production::datasets::pulumi:providers:gcp::<id>]
   + approvalWorkflow: {
       + manualApprovals: {
           + requireApproverJustification: false
           + steps                       : []
         }
     }
   + approvalWorkflow: {
       + manualApprovals: {
           + requireApproverJustification: false
           + steps                       : []
         }
     }
```

This update sets `approval_workflow` to None which is the recommended way in the pulumi docs: https://www.pulumi.com/registry/packages/gcp/api-docs/privilegedaccessmanager/entitlement/#approval_workflow_python


The other change to to set `delete_before_replace` to True which seems to be required if any updates are made to entitlements that result in resource replacement: https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-google/issues/18768

